;; ── Foresight-layer tool candidates (added 2026-06-10) ───────────────

(f/candidate :list_candidates
  :label   "list_candidates — expose f/candidate backlog as a queryable tool"
  :cluster :cluster-foresight
  :added   "2026-06-10"
  :status  :hoisted
  :scores  {:feasibility 9 :elegance 8 :containment 9 :value 8}
  :conditions ["CnjCandidateForm added to cnj-model.ts"
               "at least nine f/candidates exist in conjurer-mcp.cnj so the tool
                has a real backlog to operate on"]
  :rationale "f/candidate forms are first-class design artefacts but the prior server
              had no way to query them — retrieving the backlog required reading the raw
              .cnj file manually. A dedicated tool surfaces the candidates grouped by
              :cluster and ranked by score, making the foresight layer queryable in the
              same session that surfaces retrieval, validation, and planning results.
              Deferred until CnjCandidateForm landed in the shared model and the backlog
              was large enough that a grouped view added value over reading the file.")

(f/candidate :f-trajectory
  :label   "f/trajectory — scored trajectory analytics for a candidate"
  :cluster :cluster-foresight
  :added   "2026-06-10"
  :status  :proposed
  :scores  {:feasibility 7 :elegance 9 :containment 8 :value 7}
  :rationale "f/reassess is the grimoire's core contribution — the scored trajectory
              preserving how judgment moved, not just where it landed. But CnjCandidateForm
              does not yet extract :history; list_candidates returns only original scores
              and the trajectory is invisible to every tool. The tool would compute
              per-dimension delta and velocity (score-change / elapsed-days) and surface
              days_since_last_assessment for stale-judgment detection — all pure arithmetic
              over the model. Deferred because no workspace yet has f/reassess entries to
              run against; adding it now would add dead infrastructure with no data to
              validate the output shape."
  :conditions ["at least one f/candidate in the workspace carries a non-empty :history"
               "CnjReassessment type and CnjCandidateForm.history field added to cnj-model.ts"])

(f/candidate :lens-hoist-readiness
  :label   "lens_hoist_readiness — pre-decision triage briefing"
  :cluster :cluster-foresight
  :added   "2026-06-10"
  :status  :hoisted
  :scores  {:feasibility 8 :elegance 9 :containment 9 :value 8}
  :rationale "The grimoire states the foresight→r/decide handoff explicitly: a set of
              mature candidates becomes the alternative set a decision evaluates.
              Today that handoff is manual — the agent calls list_candidates, inspects
              scores and status, reads conditions, and reasons about readiness, all of
              which is mechanical threshold work the server should absorb. The tool
              applies deterministic structural criteria (score ≥ min_score, status active,
              conditions returned verbatim) and returns a structured pre-decision briefing
              without claiming to know whether conditions are actually met — that judgment
              stays with the practitioner. Deferred only until the backlog grows large
              enough that multi-candidate triage becomes a real cost; with nine candidates
              today the benefit is marginal."
  :conditions ["backlog contains five or more :proposed or :planned candidates"
               "at least one candidate has been reassessed (f/reassess present) so the
                has_reassessment signal in the briefing is non-trivially true"])

(f/candidate :trace-hoist-chain
  :label   "trace_hoist_chain — forward traceability from candidate to decision"
  :cluster :cluster-foresight
  :added   "2026-06-10"
  :status  :proposed
  :scores  {:feasibility 6 :elegance 9 :containment 7 :value 6}
  :rationale "f/hoist records a :into binding — the candidate references the decision
              it became — but the server neither models f/hoist forms nor can verify
              that the :into reference resolves to a real charter decision. A dangling
              hoist (candidate promoted, no receiving decision recorded) is the foresight
              equivalent of a broken :references link; surfacing it enforces the
              opening/closing symmetry the grimoire names as central. The tool also
              enables project archaeology: an agent re-entering a project can call
              trace_hoist_chain to reconstruct the idea→decision arc for the full
              workspace history. Feasibility is 6 because :into carries a symbolic
              keyword reference (e.g. :charter-decision/list-candidates-2026-06-10)
              whose resolution against charter.decisions entries requires convention-aware
              matching, not a literal key lookup — and that convention is not yet
              formalised. Deferred until the :into reference format is stable across
              at least two hoists."
  :conditions ["CnjHoist type and CnjDocument.hoists field added to cnj-model.ts"
               "at least two f/hoist forms exist in the workspace so dangling-hoist
                detection can be validated against a real case"
               ":into reference format convention formalised (keyword vs string, path convention)"])

(f/candidate :diff-candidates
  :label   "diff_candidates — semantic backlog diff between two .cnj snapshots"
  :cluster :cluster-b
  :added   "2026-06-10"
  :status  :hoisted
  :scores  {:feasibility 9 :elegance 8 :containment 9 :value 7}
  :rationale "diff_cnj computes semantic diffs over charter, targets, and assets but
              is silent on the candidates layer, even though f/candidate forms are as
              structurally significant as any other model element and their lifecycle
              changes (status promotions, score shifts, hoists) are exactly the
              what-changed-in-the-design question diff_cnj was built for. Candidates
              carry a stable :id by grimoire specification, making the diff unambiguous —
              unlike decisions (keyed by date+text fingerprint), candidates have a
              genuine stable key. The diff covers: candidates added, candidates removed,
              status changes, score deltas on shared candidates, and graduations
              (candidate in A, corresponding f/hoist in B). High feasibility because
              diff_cnj already exists as the structural pattern and the :id key makes
              the comparison trivial. Deferred because diff_cnj is most useful against
              two independently evolved snapshots — git history is the natural source —
              and the workflow for loading two-snapshot diffs is not yet formalised."
  :conditions ["diff_cnj stable with no active rework planned for tools/diff.ts"
               "CnjHoist type added to the model (needed for graduation detection —
                shared condition with trace-hoist-chain)"])

(f/candidate :lens-foresight-health
  :label   "lens_foresight_health — backlog maintenance diagnostics"
  :cluster :cluster-foresight
  :added   "2026-06-10"
  :status  :hoisted
  :scores  {:feasibility 7 :elegance 9 :containment 9 :value 8}
  :rationale "The grimoire's best-practices section names its own failure modes by name:
              the rotting backlog, rationale-free deferral, orphaned hoists. These are
              structurally checkable without any LLM and without spec lookups — pure
              arithmetic and string operations over the model. The checks: (1) stale
              candidates (no f/reassess, days_since_added > threshold); (2) rationale-thin
              candidates (:rationale absent or below minimum length); (3) orphaned hoists
              (f/hoist whose :of has no matching f/candidate :id); (4) lifecycle
              distribution (counts by :status across the workspace — a project where
              nothing leaves :proposed is using the backlog as a graveyard);
              (5) high-score / no-conditions gap (total ≥ 30 with empty :conditions,
              turning a vague 'later' into an accountable gap). This is lint_conventions
              for the foresight layer: the grimoire's own stated discipline made
              queryable as structured violations. Feasibility is 7 because it is gated
              on both the f/reassess and f/hoist model work; once those land, the
              checks themselves are trivial. Deferred in that order."
  :conditions ["CnjReassessment type and CnjCandidateForm.history added (shared with f-trajectory)"
               "CnjHoist type and CnjDocument.hoists added (shared with trace-hoist-chain)"
               "backlog is large enough (eight or more candidates) that health metrics
                are non-trivially meaningful"])
